# Attempt record

Import VerdictRecord from "./verdict_record.lg".

One model call and what became of it, and a lemma of the shared library. Both
carry lists or nested records, so the derive gives them encoders and the
decoders are written by hand in `records_decode.lg` (see `LOGOS_ISSUES.md`,
issue 1).

## Note
An attempt: who asked which model under which strategy, the hashes of what was
asked, answered and checked, the approach it took, and the verdict and cost.

## An Attempt has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a unitId, which is Text.
    a problemId, which is Text.
    a contributor, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a strategyId, which is Text.
    a promptSha, which is Text.
    a responseSha, which is Text.
    a documentSha, which is Text.
    an approachFingerprint, which is Text.
    a verdict, which is Verdict.
    a costMicros, which is Int.
    a startedAt, which is Int.
    a finishedAt, which is Int.

## Note
A lemma, deduplicated by the hash of its statement: `verified` when its proof
passed the policy, `retracted` if the verifier withdraws it. An axiom a
decomposition leaves open is a child node, not a lemma.

## A Lemma has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a name, which is Text.
    a statement, which is Text.
    a statementSha, which is Text.
    a problemId, which is Text.
    a documentSha, which is Text.
    a status, which is Text.
    an axioms, which is Seq of Text.
